# ABP GUID Generation

## Using IGuidGenerator
```csharp
public class BookManager : DomainService
{
    public Book CreateBook(string name)
    {
        var id = GuidGenerator.Create(); // Use inherited GuidGenerator
        return new Book(id, name);
    }
}
```

## Why Use IGuidGenerator?
- Generates sequential GUIDs for better database performance
- Especially important for clustered indexes
- Don't use `Guid.NewGuid()` in entity constructors

## Entity Constructor Pattern
```csharp
public class Book : AggregateRoot<Guid>
{
    public string Name { get; private set; }

    protected Book() { } // For ORM

    public Book(Guid id, string name) : base(id)
    {
        Name = name;
    }
}

// Creating entity
var book = new Book(GuidGenerator.Create(), "My Book");
```
